            <ArticleTitle>Primary ovarian choriocarcinoma presenting with acute abdomen mimicking an ectopic pregnancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>425-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A young lady presented with signs and symptoms of ectopic pregnancy. Initial BhCG was 1110.5 IU/l dropped to 18.5 IU/l postoperatively. Ovarian biopsy taken at the time of laparoscopy confirmed the diagnosis of ovarian choriocarcinoma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
